  "key_insights": [
    "Zero-Inflation Quantile Collapse: Because 78.9% of training rows and 81.85% of test rows have DailyDemand=0, the unconditional 75th percentile is 0 on almost all days. Thus unconditional Quantile_0.75 predicts near-zero everywhere (overage cost=$4,407.65, volume fill rate=0.17%), yielding high stockout cost ($10,017,640.62) under Retail Standard (Cu=3, Co=1).",
    "Two-Stage Hurdle Newsvendor Optimization: Conditioning the quantile regressor on positive demand (Y > 0) and tuning the probability cutoff on validation achieves the lowest test cost across every scenario: $7,607,741.48 in Retail Standard (Cu=3, Co=1) and $17,142,108.72 in Premium Loyalty (Cu=9, Co=1).",
    "Under Premium Loyalty (Cu=9, Co=1), both Hurdle_Newsvendor_Opt ($17,142,108.72) and Quantile_0.90 ($16,584,505.54) substantially beat Lag1_Baseline ($24,313,885.00) and symmetric TwoStageDemand ($20,166,634.12).",
    "Service Level vs Volume Fill Rate: Because 81.85% of test days have zero demand, predicting 0 everywhere trivially gives an 81.85% 'no-stockout day rate' while delivering 0% volume fill rate. Therefore both positive_day_service_level_pct and volume_fill_rate_pct are reported to prevent misleading service-level claims."
  ]
}